  "id": "t13-quota-error-kind-retry-after-zero-boundary",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 20 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 15/L15, assertion 39): a 429 that survives every SDK retry surfaces error_kind:\"quota_exhausted\" with retry_after taken from the response's own retry-after header — a positive value passes through as a Python-style float (never a bare integer: 1 must render as 1.0), a ZERO value is the exclusive boundary that collapses to null (seconds if seconds > 0 else None), an absent header is the same null, and a value that isn't parseable as a delay (an HTTP-date string) also collapses to null. HTTP 500 is the contrast case: same shape, error_kind stays null. Five sub-cases, one per spawned child, mirroring the T13 baseline's own measured evidence (evidence-s05b-quota.json): retry-after:0, no header, HTTP 500 (contrast), retry-after:1, retry-after as an HTTP-date. KNOWN LIMIT (declared, not a gap to fix): the NUMBER of upstream attempts before giving up is out of scope for T13 (contract: \"O numero de tentativas do SDK antes de desistir e fronteira T10; fixa-lo como paridade T13 e rejeicao pelo criterio 8.19\") and is NOT byte-comparable here — measured during this ticket's own investigation, the candidate's transport (src/transports/client.ts) retries only status>=500, never 429, so it reaches its final quota_exhausted classification after exactly ONE upstream attempt per 429 case, while the oracle's real SDK retries a 429 up to its own budget (measured: 3 total attempts, matching its own 500 behavior) before the unparseable-date case, where it also gives up after exactly one attempt. events.summary (upstream request count) is therefore excluded from comparisons on purpose; escalated separately as a candidate-side gap in T10's own retry policy, out of this ticket's authority to fix. Every child's FINAL observable envelope (error_kind/retry_after/output, the field this assertion is actually about) is asserted byte-exact regardless of how many attempts either side took to get there.",
